# The programs of the second adversarial review of zv-own (docs/reviews/own-2.md): the `bad*` mistakes that 0.17.13 called clean, the
# `ok*` programs that it reported, and the controls. A `bad*` is an error, an `ok*` is clean.
# badInitBufferReturn reads the byte before the list goes: correct, clean. badPqSift, badPdqSift and badPqPopMoves are
# data dependent (a heap sifts one element, which one depends on the values): the checker counts the pointer as maybe stale
# and does not report it (tools/run_own.sh checks the count).
review2.badAdoptFreeThenDeinit error
review2.badAdoptFreeUse error
review2.badAdoptGrowFree error
review2.badAdoptGrowUse error
review2.badAdoptSelfSlice error
review2.badArenaByValue error
